# K05 v7 look (owner, 2026-11-03: "the lighting effect looks very basic", "the laser effect looks very low res"),
# read by queue-nov3b.sh p3 (one flag per line). From previews out/k05v7/{a_v6,b_rake,c_low,d_v7}: the key pool drops
# low (0.30 m) and comes from the crown end (0.70, 0.40) in a 16 deg cone at 260 W, so a long raking gradient crosses
# the head and picks out the tow relief, the throat side in deep shade (fill 3, was 11); the coat band dimmer (120 -> 22; 35 still read as a white bar)
# so it stays a band, not a white glare; a brighter rim hairline (8 -> 14) draws the outline; the plate a shade darker
# (amb 0.20); the laser a little stronger with more glow (26, 2.4). Resolution: 5120 x 2880 (the 0.16 mm line is about
# 1.2 px there, a crisp line on a 5K screen; at 2560 it was upscaled x2.16).
--wp_z 0.30
--wp_x 0.70
--wp_y 0.40
--wp_deg 16
--wpool 260
--wfill 9
--face 0
--rim 14
--amb 0.20
--glow 2.4
--laser 26
# v7c (cloud REQUEST K05-command-fix, owner 2026-11-06 "this doesn't look right"; supersedes v7b's card alone), every
# item checked on previews out/k05b/fix_a, fix_b, fix_p, fix_p2:
#  1 white across the whole face: lw_card (a soft overhead spot over the crown-side half, diffuse only, head only,
#    Command only: 45 W at 0.14, -0.10, 0.55 m, 40 deg) and the fill back to 9 W (was 3): display face luma about 160
#    at 2560 (v6 149, v7 125), the face reads as the same white as the rim, throat and handle
#  2 the coat band (lg_face, the hard vertical stripe down the left third and over the throat) off: --face 0
#  3+4 the laser breaks at every hole (--hole_break 1: no hits on the bores or the stone seen through a hole) and the
#    widest halo scale is dropped (--glow_wide 0: at 16 mm it filled the crossed hole with red)
#  5 no profile wake beside the line (--nprof 0): only the crisp scan line
#  6 dark holes: no stone patch under the hole field (--holefloor 0; its granite flecks read as sparkle in the bores)
#    and an indirect clamp (--clamp 4)
#  7 Naked (kit, not a flag): K01's HD weave on the bare handle (k789_lib.naked_neck_hd) and KQ_NAKED_FLARE=0 (req-nov6.sh)
--wcard 45
--hole_break 1
--nprof 0
--glow_wide 0
--holefloor 0
--clamp 4
# K05-throat (cloud REQUEST 2026-11-07, owner "make the face beside the throat brighter too", Command only; previews
# out/k05t/a..e): lw_card2, a second soft overhead spot, diffuse only, head only, from the handle side and the camera
# side (-0.30, -0.20, 0.40 m, 22 deg, 32 W; overhead at 20 W it mirrored in the twill's sheen as a streak): the throat
# wedge reads 158 against 171 for the rest of the face at 2560 (v7c 124 against 157), the neck 135 (was 96). The line
# tapers to 15 % over the last 3.5 mm before each hole lip (--hb_fade, --hb_floor), so its halo no longer lands as a
# pink blob on the lip.
--wcard2 32
--wc2_x -0.30
--wc2_y -0.20
--wc2_z 0.40
--wc2_deg 22
--hb_fade 3.5
--hb_floor 0.15
